+          // Require a canonical DigestInfo encoding. asn1.validate() above
+          // confirms the structure but tolerates anything it was not asked
+          // to check: extra elements in either SEQUENCE, a NULL parameters
+          // field carrying content bytes, and non-minimal long-form length
+          // octets all leave attacker-controlled slack bytes inside the
+          // DigestInfo, enabling low-exponent PKCS#1 v1.5 signature forgery
+          // (CVE-2026-85393). Re-encode the expected DigestInfo from the
+          // parsed OID and digest and require a byte-for-byte match, which
+          // rejects all of those variants at once. Both DigestAlgorithm
+          // forms that occur in practice are accepted: with NULL parameters
+          // (as encoded by forge and OpenSSL) and, for the algorithms that
+          // permit it, without them. The comparison is a prefix comparison
+          // so that the unsupported _parseAllDigestBytes testing flag keeps
